    "body": "## Result\n\nNegative answer to Janssen's non-ACM gap-one line-configuration question, over every algebraically closed field: any nonempty reduced finite union of lines with alpha(I^(2))=alpha(I)+1 is coplanar or a complete pseudostar and hence ACM.\n\n## Proof and review\n\n- Complete characteristic-free adjoint/conductor proof in PUBLIC_TURN_2.md\n- Separate full adversarial AI review: PASS_COMPLETE_ARBITRARY_CHARACTERISTIC_LINE_THEOREM\n- 3,888 exact supplemental algebra controls, including characteristic 2 edge cases\n- Two substantive recovered author turns; only the existing target QUEUE row changes to claimed_solved 2/5\n- First-turn partial checkpoint preserved byte-for-byte and retained in commit ancestry; the earlier characteristic-zero scope correction remains visible\n\nClassical inputs and existing pseudostar results are credited. The claim covers the source's line question, not arbitrary reduced curves. This is AI-assisted work and separate AI review, not human peer review or formal certification. Novelty and priority are not certified. No merge, release, DOI publication or external contact is requested.\n",
